{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"standard-hyperbolic-marabou","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe graph loader/BFS centralization (985c-32d2-e828-4e6a, Gerrit 1708) named two behaviours as explicit helpers that had previously been inline. The rebar code-review bot flagged both as untested. The gaps are PRE-EXISTING — the same logic was uncovered while inline — but naming them made them visible.\n\n## Gaps\n1. `_graph.py::_is_at_level` — the target-side level guard in `check_cycle_at_level` refuses to traverse into a neighbour whose `ticket_type` differs from the queried level. Every existing `check_cycle_at_level` test in tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py uses a single uniform level, so the cross-level refusal is never exercised: a regression that dropped the guard would keep the suite green.\n2. `_unblock.py::_load_states_with_tombstones` — three behaviours have no test driving them through `detect_newly_unblocked`: (a) a dir whose reduce returns None but which has a `.tombstone.json` yields a status-only stub, (b) a present tombstone's status OVERRIDES the reduced status, (c) a malformed/unreadable tombstone degrades to `deleted` rather than to 'no tombstone'.\n\n## Approach\nAdd characterization tests only — no production change. Follow the pattern of `test_get_all_blocked_by_accumulates_targets_without_a_ticket_dir` (added by 985c): assert the behaviour that exists today, so the tests pin the contract rather than propose a new one.\n\n- tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py: a tracker where an epic-level cycle is only closable via a task-level neighbour, asserting `check_cycle_at_level(..., level='epic')` returns False because the cross-level hop is refused.\n- tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py: one test per tombstone behaviour (a)/(b)/(c), driven through the public `detect_newly_unblocked` rather than the private helper.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A test fails if `_is_at_level`'s target-side level check is removed from `_same_level_neighbors` (verified by deleting the guard locally and observing the new test go red).\n- [ ] A test fails if the tombstone-status override in `_load_states_with_tombstones` is removed.\n- [ ] A test fails if the reduce-returns-None + tombstone-present stub branch is removed.\n- [ ] A test fails if the malformed-tombstone fallback stops defaulting to `deleted`.\n- [ ] No file under src/rebar is modified (verified: `git diff --name-only` lists only test files).\n- [ ] make lint and make typecheck are green.","id":"defc-658e-bfe1-4cab","parent_id":"2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07","priority":2,"tags":["remediation","tests","ae1b"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Cover graph traversal seams surfaced by the loader/BFS refactor"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786602715615909001,"uuid":"774c19a6-4434-436f-a7a0-4708753fee27"}